================================================================================
2. What the tools produce - GPL-2.0
================================================================================

This repository ships no kernel source. The scripts download the driver sources
matching your running kernel from github.com/arduino/linux-qcom at build time,
and the tools in tools/ modify them in place.

Those sources are GPL-2.0, so the patched drivers you build and install are
GPL-2.0 as well. Some of the changes the tools apply are adapted from the
Raspberry Pi kernel tree (github.com/raspberrypi/linux), also GPL-2.0:

  tools/patch-edt-ft5x06.py         polling fallback and released-contact
                                    tracking, from RPi's edt-ft5x06 driver
  tools/patch-attiny-regulator.py   cached is_enabled(), from RPi's
                                    rpi-panel-attiny-regulator driver
  tools/gen-panel-patch.py          the emitted panel descriptor follows the
                                    panel-simple conventions in the Linux tree

If you redistribute a built kernel module, or a modified copy of the driver
sources these tools generate, you must do so under GPL-2.0 and provide the
corresponding source. The generator scripts themselves stay MIT.

Full text: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.txt

================================================================================
3. Panel timings
================================================================================

The timings in panels/waveshare-800x480.panel are taken from the device tree
overlay vc4-kms-dsi-waveshare-800x480-overlay.dts in the Raspberry Pi kernel
tree (GPL-2.0/MIT dual-licensed, as are the arch/arm/boot/dts overlays there).
They describe how the hardware behaves and are reproduced here as fact.
